<%#
  Read-only per-hoojah vote distribution. Local: dist (a UserAnalytics::Distribution).

  The bar markup is copied — NOT shared — from hujahs/_vote_bars: that partial is
  welded to a button_to vote form, this one only reads. Extracting a common bar partial
  was considered and rejected in Slice 5 and again in Slice 9 Task 4.7: the seam is four
  lines of markup, and the shared version would have to carry a "with buttons / without
  buttons" flag through the one widget in the product that must never sprout a control
  it wasn't asked for. Below k=5 total votes the split is suppressed ("fewer than 5
  votes") instead of rendering the numbers — a privacy floor from Slice 5 (UserAnalytics::K),
  not styling. Do not soften the copy and do not make the branch conditional on anything.

  DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.7) —
  docs/design-system/components/analytics/DistributionBar.prompt.md ("read-only bars, no
  buttons") plus readme.md VISUAL FOUNDATIONS on bars: "8px tall rounded track `#e5e7eb`,
  stance-colored fill by %, percentage label right-aligned". The three rows already were
  that and are byte-identical to `_vote_bars`' track/label half on purpose — the two
  widgets are the same bar and must stay pixel-identical even though they are two files.

  What changed is the surface. It was a hand-written
  `rounded border border-gray-100 bg-white px-4 py-3`; it is now `ui/_card`, so the 4px
  rounding and the grey outline go and the card `shadow` arrives. Card.prompt.md forbids
  rounding a card outright and puts `#f3f4f6` on internal hairlines (`ui/_divider`), never
  on a card's own edge. The stack gap moves 12px → `mb-2` (8px), which is the DS's
  "Cards stack with 8px gaps on a white page" and what `hujahs/_hujah_card` already uses.
  `last:mb-0` stays: the row of cards is the last thing on the page and the trailing
  margin would double up against `main`'s `py-6`.

  `padded:` carries the padding and `class:` carries only margin — never both padding
  routes at once, per the same-family ordering trap documented on `ui/_card`.

  Stance names are interpolated into `text-` and `bg-`, which the Tailwind scanner cannot
  see; both prefixes over the stance trio are covered by the `@source inline(...)`
  safelist in app/assets/tailwind/application.css. A NEW interpolated prefix here means a
  new entry there.
%>
<%
  rows = [["agree", dist.agree, dist.agree_pct],
    ["neutral", dist.neutral, dist.neutral_pct],
    ["disagree", dist.disagree, dist.disagree_pct]]
%>
<%= render layout: "ui/card", locals: {padded: true, class: "mb-2 last:mb-0"} do %>
  <p class="text-sm text-black mb-2 line-clamp-2"><%= strip_tags(dist.body) %></p>
  <% if dist.suppressed? %>
    <p class="text-xs text-light-grey">fewer than 5 votes</p>
  <% else %>
    <% rows.each do |stance, count, pct| %>
      <div class="flex items-center mb-2 last:mb-0">
        <small class="w-16 text-<%= stance %>"><%= stance.capitalize %></small>
        <div class="flex-1 mx-3 h-2 bg-gray-200 rounded overflow-hidden">
          <div class="h-2 rounded bg-<%= stance %>" style="width: <%= pct %>%"></div>
        </div>
        <small class="w-10 text-right text-<%= stance %>"><%= pct %>%</small>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  <% end %>
<% end %>
